# /etc/hunter/keys — the Ed25519 keys hunter checks signed feeds with.
#
# Read by the kernel at boot, before the feeds in /etc/hunter/signatures.d/,
# as a script in hunter's control language (all or nothing, like
# policy.conf). One line per publisher:
#
#   feed-key <name> <64 hex digits: the Ed25519 public key>
#
# `hunterctl trust-key <name> <hex>` adds a key to the running system and
# here. A feed in /etc/hunter/feeds names the key it must be signed with as a
# fourth field. The publisher makes the key and signs with it on another
# machine, with tools/hunterctl/hunter-feed-sign from the Eclipse OS sources:
#
#   hunter-feed-sign keygen feeds.pem mirror     # prints the feed-key line
#
# Once hunter is sealed no key can be added, and a name never changes its key
# until reboot.
